      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "YES, i love this though my idea was a bit different from it not showing on update, I think a way for the creator to Stage content to be pushed would be amazing. In my head it would kind of go something like this, I'd tell my build and publish to stage on pc side and on quest side, Then I'd log into vrchat.com and tell the map to update when I was ready. It's very frustrating as a game world creator to have my games not work because of un equal code!",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2021-11-22T19:27:51.557Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Here's generally what happens when I update my world :\n- I upload my world for PC\n- It appears in the recently updated worlds.\n- Quest and PC users join my world, since Quest users are on a different world version the world is broken for them.\n- I start uploading the Quest version.\n- Once it's done, I basically always need to join a public instance to tell anyone that the world just got updated, and that a new instance needs to be created if it is currently broken for them.\nSo it would be nice to have a checkbox \"Show in updated worlds\", I would only check it if the upload for PC and Quest is  finished, or when I do a major update (for instance no need to show my world in the recently updated one if I just fixed one texture...).",
